      "why": "iterative is the minimum-area CORDIC family (single shared datapath, barrel shifters, no parallel micro-rotation chains). It will almost certainly win on luts_plus_ffs, which is the selection objective. However, it produces one result every N+3 cycles (~17-21 cycles), so its raw throughput is ~25-30 Msps at 500 MHz, which may fall just short of the 32 Msps constraint. I include it to map the area/accuracy corner of the Pareto front and to confirm whether it can meet throughput at the Fmax the cost model predicts. If it fails throughput, it still anchors the low-area end of the front for hypervolume. N=14-18, W=16, angle_guard -1..0, frac_guard 0..2 covers the accuracy requirement with minimal area."
    }
